  "limitations": [
    "Replay uses a prior successful focused test as hypothetical registration; explicit registration, source/test hashes, environment identity and tree epoch are unobserved. Actual state machine requires trusted guards; deployment credit is zero.",
    "Only bounded static single-source edits, exact python py_compile and exact registered test argv/cwd are supported. No guessed tests or added unsolicited intermediate steps receive match credit.",
    "All matched compile calls overlap the prior edit-compile candidate; only exact subsequent focused-test calls are a new stage. Deduplicate target call keys in any conservative union.",
    "Complete-chain usage includes both stages and must not be added again to first/second-stage totals.",
    "Failed compile stops the workflow; test failures remain failures, not successful fixes. Tests may mutate artifacts, so runner must define permitted cache/output writes separately.",
    "At most two tool calls and 130 seconds per workflow, with 16KB compile and 32KB test output caps. Unmatched proposals and possible extra test executions add cost rather than savings.",
    "Proposed max tool-call count assumes every compile succeeds, not an estimate of actual runtime calls. No runtime/output token costs were measured.",
    "No historical filesystem state reconstructed, commands executed, model calls made or bug outcomes validated.",
    "Matching responses may contain needed reasoning; gross recorded usage is not net savings. Router, guard-hash, execution, false-positive, downstream context/cache and reasoning-loss costs are excluded.",
    "Cache and reasoning are subsets of input/output totals; no double counting."
  ]
